WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:29.007
Danny: We’ve got to find a way to see in!

2
00:00:29.008 --> 00:00:41.220
Let’s go this way.

3
00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:45.524
Brad: The guards are everywhere.

4
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:48.651
Danny: If only they would move somewhere else.

5
00:00:48.652 --> 00:00:50.816
Brad: That’s it!

6
00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.176
Danny: What?

7
00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:54.842
Brad: We could make a noise back near the gate.

8
00:00:54.843 --> 00:00:58.567
Brad: Maybe the guards will run to see what it is.

9
00:00:58.568 --> 00:01:02.870
Danny: Great idea. One of us could throw a pebble.

10
00:01:02.871 --> 00:01:05.708
Brad: All the pebbles are bigger than us.

11
00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:08.158
But this grain of sand should work.

12
00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:10.682
Brad: Who has the strongest arm?

13
00:01:10.683 --> 00:01:13.369
Danny: Tina.

14
00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.961
Brad: Well, she’s not here.

15
00:01:15.962 --> 00:01:19.912
Danny: I know. We’ll have to throw it together.

16
00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:27.822
Brad: Teamwork always works for us.

17
00:01:27.823 --> 00:01:30.302
Brad: One, two . . .

18
00:01:30.303 --> 00:01:37.337
Danny: Three!

19
00:01:37.338 --> 00:01:39.141
Mite 1: Hey! Did you hear that?

20
00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:40.960
Mite 2: We should check it out!

21
00:01:40.961 --> 00:01:48.523
Mite 1: Get the other guards!

22
00:01:48.524 --> 00:01:50.951
Brad: Perfect! Let’s go!

23
00:01:50.952 --> 00:01:54.036
It won’t be long before the guards come back.

24
00:01:54.037 --> 00:01:56.399
Danny: I see some bottle caps.

25
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.719
Maybe we could stack them.

26
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:06.957
Brad: It’s worth a try.

27
00:02:06.958 --> 00:02:09.639
Brad: This isn’t going to work.

28
00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.187
Danny: Hey, there’s a straw over there.

29
00:02:13.188 --> 00:02:14.970
Brad: How big?

30
00:02:14.971 --> 00:02:19.216
Danny: It’s a regular-size straw. It’s big!

31
00:02:19.217 --> 00:02:23.479
Brad: Geez, I never thought a straw could look so big!

32
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.335
Danny: It’s long enough to reach the top of the wall.

33
00:02:27.336 --> 00:02:30.124
Brad: Do you think we can lift it?

34
00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:42.034
Danny: That’s the great thing about straws: they’re light.

35
00:02:42.035 --> 00:02:46.707
Brad: Careful, careful.

36
00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:53.380
Brad: Okay, now turn it.

37
00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:55.214
Danny: There, we did it!

38
00:02:55.215 --> 00:02:57.855
Brad: Okay, I’m going to climb up.

39
00:02:57.856 --> 00:03:02.635
Danny: You? But you’re not good at climbing!

40
00:03:02.636 --> 00:03:05.183
Brad: You just hold it steady.

41
00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.702
Danny: Are you sure?

42
00:03:06.703 --> 00:03:09.428
It looks very slippery.

43
00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:12.102
Brad: If Tina were here, she would climb it.

44
00:03:12.103 --> 00:03:14.469
But it’s just you and me.

45
00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:18.668
Danny: Okay. Give it a try.

46
00:03:18.669 --> 00:03:20.156
Danny: Careful!

47
00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:24.954
Brad: I’m okay.

48
00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:28.131
Danny: What do you see?

49
00:03:28.132 --> 00:03:33.025
Brad: There are several towers and lots of mites!

50
00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:35.553
Danny: Any sign of Chuck and Dave?

51
00:03:35.554 --> 00:03:41.662
Brad: I’m looking . . .

52
00:03:41.663 --> 00:03:43.280
Brad: Oh no!

53
00:03:43.281 --> 00:03:44.622
Danny: What?

54
00:03:44.623 --> 00:03:46.516
Brad: They’re in a prison.

55
00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:49.656
We’ll never get them out!
